GETPID(2)                      P32W Unix                       GETPID(2)

NAME
       getpid, getppid - get process identification

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       pid_t getpid(void);
       pid_t getppid(void);

DESCRIPTION
       getpid returns the process ID of the calling process, and
       getppid that of its parent (1, init, once the parent has
       exited: orphans are adopted by init). A process ID is never
       reused while the system runs: they are handed out in
       increasing order from 1.

RETURN VALUE
       The ID asked for. These calls cannot fail.

SEE ALSO
       fork(2), getuid(2), kill(2), ps(1)
